<<<
Proved, not proven, is the regular

p.p., the latter being properly from

the verb preve used in Scotland

after it had given way to prove in

England; cf. weave woven, cleave

cloven. Except in the phrase not proven as a quotation from Scotch law, proven is better left alone.
===
*Proved*, not *proven*, is the regular p.p., the latter being properly from the verb *preve* used in Scotland after it had given way to *prove* in England; cf. *weave woven, cleave cloven*. Except in the phrase *not proven* as a quotation from Scotch law, *proven* is better left alone.
>>>

